message: "If you use this repository, please cite the versioned software release and the accompanying manuscript."
title: "Endpoint Coordinate: Lean 4 Formalization"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: 2026-09-28
authors:
  - family-names: "Małmyga"
    given-names: "Paweł"
repository-code: "https://github.com/pawelmalmyga-ai/EndpointCoordinate"
url: "https://github.com/pawelmalmyga-ai/EndpointCoordinate"
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 formalization of an exponentially weighted endpoint coordinate for
  time series, including exact finite-path geometry, the classical Wilder
  recursion and RSI/log-odds bridge, exact Wilder effective length, Gaussian
  and Laplace benchmarks, algebraic checks of defined Student-t calibration
  formulas, and a finite-variance central limit theorem for normalized linear
  Wilder rows. Separate artifacts provide a symbolic coefficient audit, a
  conventional heavy-tail technical note, and a reproducible numerical
  normality study. Those artifacts are clearly distinguished from Lean
  theorems.
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
  - exponential smoothing
  - effective sample size
  - log-odds
  - RSI
  - central limit theorem
  - numerical normality audit
